module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AffineBaseCoveringSieveStepOne
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Fpqc.SheafConditionDisjointUnion

/-!
# The base change along a finite coproduct chart, glued from the members of the chart

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsEffectiveAffineDescentAlongFpqc` and the chart it consumes,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_affine_chart_of_finite_fpqc`, deliver their conclusion one
member of the covering family at a time: for each `i` the base change of `f : X ⟶ Y` along
`yoneda.map (w i) ≫ h` is representable with `P`. What Stacks 041Z needs is the same statement
for the *single* refining morphism `q : c ⟶ a` out of the coproduct of the family. This file
performs that passage.

Only Zariski gluing is involved. The injections `inj i : W i ⟶ c` of a finite coproduct cofan of
the site are open immersions on underlying schemes, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_iso_sigma_of_isColimit_cofan`, and their images cover `c`;
so the per-member data exhibits `X ×[Y] yoneda.obj c` as a sheaf covered by finitely many
representable open subfunctors, which glues by Tag 01JJ. No fpqc descent of a *scheme* is
performed here — that is what `IsEffectiveAffineDescentAlongFpqc` has already done for each
member — so nothing below depends on Stacks 0APL.

## Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheaf_pullback_snd_cofanDesc_of_finite`: if the base change of
  `f : X ⟶ Y` along `yoneda.map (w i) ≫ h` is representable with `P` for every member `w i` of a
  finite family which factors through the morphism `q : c ⟶ a` out of a coproduct cofan of the
  sources, then the base change of `f` along `yoneda.map q ≫ h` is representable with `P`.

## Implementation notes

*The three steps.* They are those of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coveringSieveBody_affineBase_of_affineFlatSource`, with the chart's
coproduct handed over rather than constructed. First
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isPullback_restrict_of_presheaf` turns the datum over `W i` into
a representable open subfunctor `yoneda.obj (W' i) ⟶ X ×[Y] yoneda.obj c` over `inj i`. Then
`AlgebraicGeometry.isRepresentable_of_zariskiCover_of_size_le` — Tag 01JJ under a uniform size
bound — glues those subfunctors; the index type is finite, so both of its cardinal hypotheses
are free, the uniform bound being the supremum of finitely many sizes of objects of the site.
Finally `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheaf_of_coveringSieve_of_descendsAlong` recovers `P` on the
descended morphism, applied to the covering sieve generated by the injections.

*Why the property transfers to an arbitrary arrow of that sieve.* The hypothesis here is weaker
than the one that statement consumes: it is given for the members of the family only, not for
every arrow of the sieve they generate. An arrow of `CategoryTheory.Sieve.ofArrows W inj`
factors as `g₁ ≫ inj i`, and the base change of `f` along `yoneda.map (g₁ ≫ inj i) ≫ yoneda.map q
≫ h` is the base change along `yoneda.map g₁` of the base change along
`yoneda.map (inj i) ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h`; so the gap is closed by
`CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange`, which needs nothing of `P`.

*The index type is reindexed, not bounded.* The family is indexed by an arbitrary finite
`ι : Type v`, while Tag 01JJ in the shape used here asks for an index type in the site's own
universe. A finite type is in bijection with some `Fin n` by `Finite.exists_equiv_fin`, and
`ULift (Fin n)` lives in every universe, so that is the index type the glueing is run over. No
cardinal hypothesis on the site is incurred: `#(ULift (Fin n)) ≤ ℵ₀ < B.cutoff` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.aleph0_lt_cutoff`, and the uniform size bound is the supremum of
finitely many sizes of objects of the site.

*Nothing is tagged.* The statement is a step inside Stacks 041Z, not any of its parts, and the
tags of the pieces it composes already sit on those pieces. In particular `@[stacks 041Z]` is
**not** placed here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 041Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/041Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01JJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01JJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02W8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03KC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03KC)
-/

@[expose] public section

open Cardinal CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u v

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
  {X Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (f : X ⟶ Y)

/-- **The base change along the morphism out of a finite coproduct chart is representable with
`P` as soon as the base changes along the members of the chart are.**

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of sheaves on the big fppf site of `S`, let
`h : yoneda.obj a ⟶ Y`, let `w i : W i ⟶ a` be a finite family, let `inj i : W i ⟶ c` be the
injections of a coproduct cofan of the `W i` inside the site and let `q : c ⟶ a` satisfy
`inj i ≫ q = w i`. If the base change of `f` along `yoneda.map (w i) ≫ h` is representable with
`P` for every `i`, then so is the base change of `f` along `yoneda.map q ≫ h`.

This is the passage from the per-member conclusion of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsEffectiveAffineDescentAlongFpqc` to the single-morphism conclusion
that Stacks 041Z consumes, and it is pure Zariski gluing: the cofan injections are open
immersions on underlying schemes covering `c`, so the restricted data are representable open
subfunctors of `X ×[Y] yoneda.obj c` covering it, and Tag 01JJ glues them. The property is then
recovered on the glued morphism by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheaf_of_coveringSieve_of_descendsAlong`. -/
theorem presheaf_pullback_snd_cofanDesc_of_finite {P : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}}
    [IsZariskiLocalAtTarget P]
    [P.DescendsAlong (@Surjective ⊓ @Flat ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation)]
    (hX : Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) X)
    (hY : Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) Y)
    {a : BigFppfOver B S hS} (h : yoneda.obj a ⟶ Y)
    {ι : Type v} [Finite ι] (W : ι → BigFppfOver B S hS) (w : ∀ i, W i ⟶ a)
    {c : BigFppfOver B S hS} {inj : ∀ i, W i ⟶ c}
    (hcol : IsColimit (Cofan.mk c inj)) (q : c ⟶ a) (hq : ∀ i, inj i ≫ q = w i)
    (hall : ∀ i, (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf
      (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map (w i) ≫ h))) :
    (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf
      (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map q ≫ h)) := by
  classical
  have _ := MorphismProperty.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange
    (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)) (F := yoneda)
  -- transporting the datum along an equality of the morphism it is taken over
  have hcongr : ∀ {b : BigFppfOver B S hS} (g₁ g₂ : yoneda.obj b ⟶ Y), g₁ = g₂ →
      (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (pullback.snd f g₁) →
      (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (pullback.snd f g₂) := by
    intro b g₁ g₂ hg hP
    subst hg
    exact hP
  -- the cofan is a coproduct of schemes, so its injections are an open covering
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := BigFppfOver.exists_iso_sigma_of_isColimit_cofan W hcol
  have he' : ∀ i, Sigma.ι (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (W i)) i ≫ e.hom =
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (inj i) := fun i ↦ by simpa using he i
  have hinj : ∀ i, _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (inj i)) := by
    intro i
    rw [← he' i]
    infer_instance
  have hsurj : ∀ y : (∐ fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (W i) : Scheme.{u}),
      ∃ i : ι, y ∈ Set.range (Sigma.ι (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (W i)) i) :=
    fun y ↦ (sigmaOpenCover _).exists_eq y
  have hinjcov : ∀ y : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj c,
      ∃ i, y ∈ Set.range ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (inj i)).base := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨i, z, hz⟩ := hsurj (e.inv.base y)
    refine ⟨i, z, ?_⟩
    rw [← he' i, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hz, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, e.inv_hom_id]
    rfl
  -- the datum over each member, read over the coproduct
  have hpieces : ∀ i, (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf
      (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map (inj i) ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h)) := by
    intro i
    refine hcongr (yoneda.map (w i) ≫ h) _ ?_ (hall i)
    rw [← hq i, Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc]
  choose W' pr k hpb _hPpr using fun i ↦
    exists_isPullback_restrict_of_presheaf f (yoneda.map q ≫ h) (inj i) (hpieces i)
  -- reindex the charts by a type of the site's own universe
  obtain ⟨n, ⟨eι⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin ι
  set ρ : ULift.{u} (Fin n) → ι := fun j => eι.symm j.down with hρ
  have hρsurj : ∀ i, ∃ j, ρ j = i := fun i => ⟨ULift.up (eι i), by simp [hρ]⟩
  -- the pieces glue, both cardinal hypotheses of Tag 01JJ being free for a finite index type
  have hFsheaf : Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)
      (pullback f (yoneda.map q ≫ h)) :=
    BigFppfOver.isSheaf_pullback_yoneda_obj f (yoneda.map q ≫ h) hX hY
  have hI : #(ULift.{u} (Fin n)) < B.cutoff :=
    Cardinal.mk_le_aleph0.trans_lt B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
  have hμ : (Finset.univ.sup fun j =>
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (W' (ρ j))).size) < B.cutoff := by
    refine (Finset.sup_lt_iff ?_).2 fun j _ => (W' (ρ j)).left.property
    exact lt_of_le_of_lt bot_le B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
  have hWμ : ∀ j, ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (W' (ρ j))).size ≤
      Finset.univ.sup fun j => ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (W' (ρ j))).size :=
    fun j => Finset.le_sup (f := fun j : ULift.{u} (Fin n) =>
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (W' (ρ j))).size) (Finset.mem_univ j)
  have hcovρ : ∀ y : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj c, ∃ j,
      y ∈ Set.range ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (inj (ρ j))).base := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hinjcov y
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hρsurj i
    exact ⟨j, by rwa [hj]⟩
  have hrep : (pullback f (yoneda.map q ≫ h)).IsRepresentable :=
    isRepresentable_of_zariskiCover_of_size_le B S hS hFsheaf hI hμ
      (fun j => W' (ρ j)) hWμ (fun j => k (ρ j))
      (fun j => isOpenImmersion_of_isPullback_yoneda_map B S hS (hinj (ρ j)) (hpb (ρ j)))
      (isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_of_openCover B S hS
        (fun j => hinj (ρ j)) hcovρ (fun j => hpb (ρ j)))
  -- the property is recovered on the descended morphism over the coproduct
  refine presheaf_of_coveringSieve_of_descendsAlong (yoneda.map q ≫ h)
    (relativelyRepresentable_pullback_snd f (yoneda.map q ≫ h) hrep)
    (BigFppfOver.ofArrows_mem_topology_of_isOpenImmersion B S hS inj hinj hinjcov) ?_
  rintro b g ⟨Z, g₁, g₂, ⟨i⟩, hfac⟩
  have hgm : yoneda.map g = yoneda.map g₁ ≫ yoneda.map (inj i) := by
    rw [← Functor.map_comp, hfac]
  have heq : yoneda.map g ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h =
      yoneda.map g₁ ≫ yoneda.map (inj i) ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h := by
    rw [hgm, Category.assoc]
  have hbig : IsPullback
      (pullback.fst f (yoneda.map g ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h))
      (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map g ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h)) f
      (yoneda.map g₁ ≫ yoneda.map (inj i) ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h) := by
    rw [← heq]
    exact IsPullback.of_hasPullback _ _
  exact MorphismProperty.of_isPullback
    (hbig.of_right' (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f (yoneda.map (inj i) ≫ yoneda.map q ≫ h)))
    (hpieces i)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
